 'Large chunks dilute precise retrieval; tiny chunks lose conditions and context. Fixed-size chunking can cut semantic boundaries, while semantic chunking follows paragraphs and topic shifts. Small-to-big retrieval locates a child and restores its relevant parent through a stable ID. Late chunking first encodes the document at token level and pools according to chunk boundaries. Parent restoration still requires relevance checks, deduplication and a context budget.',
